299 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (This project implements a robust Speech Emotion Recognition \(SER\) system utilizing a hybrid deep learning architecture designed for cross-speaker generalization. The pipeline begins with advanced, adaptive audio preprocessing on combined RAVDESS and CREMA-D datasets, employing SNR estimation and spectral subtraction to clean low-quality audio, alongside Voice Activity Detection to segment the speech. Features are extracted as 3-channel Log-Mel Spectrograms \(Mel + Delta + Delta-Delta\) and augmented on-the-fly during training with techniques like pitch shift, time stretch, and noise injection. The core of the system is a CNN-BiLSTM-Transformer model, where the CNN extracts local features, the BiLSTM captures short-term temporal context, and the Transformer's attention mechanism models global, long-range dependencies for the final classification into six standardized emotions. The model is trained using PyTorch with an Early Stopping mechanism and rigorously evaluated using speaker-independent data splits to ensure high Accuracy and Weighted F1-Scores on the test set.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
300 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 140 0 R
/Pg 24 0 R
/A [552 0 R 0]
/K [2]
>>
endobj
301 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 140 0 R
/Pg 24 0 R
/A [553 0 R 0]
/K [3]
>>
endobj
302 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 141 0 R
/Pg 25 0 R
/A [554 0 R 0]
/K [0]
>>
endobj
303 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 141 0 R
/E (The proposed model demonstrated moderate performance in the task of Speech Emotion Recognition \(SER\). Its best overall result was a test accuracy of 57.01% \(F1 0.561\) pooled across both datasets, with 57.75% on CREMA-D alone and 52.88% on RAVDESS alone. However, it showed a clear generalization gap: accuracy dropped to 30.93% when trained on CREMA-D and cross-tested on RAVDESS, and further to 17.40% in the reverse direction \(trained on RAVDESS, tested on CREMA-D\).)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
304 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 141 0 R
/E ( In sharp contrast, the developed model \(GL-DSED\), showcased a vastly superior performance on the same core task. When tested on the EmoDB dataset, the developed model achieved an Unweighted Accuracy \(UA\) of 87.61%. This represents an improvement of roughly 30.6 percentage points compared to the proposed model's overall test accuracy.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
